# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# TV codec diag clips (stage 8, /bigscreen/diag)
# Four 1080p sample clips, one AV variable each, served by Next.js static at /samples/*.
# They are BINARIES and they do not belong in this repository; the exact ffmpeg command line
# for each one is in docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-11-tv-stage8-device-readings.md. The diag
# page renders an explicit "FILE NOT PRESENT" state when they are absent, which is the state
# this checkout is in.
# The pattern is the directory's CONTENTS (`/*`), not the directory (`/`), and that is
# load-bearing rather than style: git does not descend into an excluded directory, so with
# `/public/samples/` the negation below is unreachable and `git check-ignore` still names the
# directory line for a `.vtt` (measured, which is how this was found).
/public/samples/*
# EXCEPT the stage-9 cue probes, which are the opposite kind of artefact to the clips: two
# hand-typed WebVTT files of a few hundred bytes each, and reading 27a's whole premise is
# that they are ALREADY THERE — that arm needs no clip, no torrent and no backend precisely
# so a blank screen has one candidate cause. A probe file nobody has copied over is a second.
!/public/samples/*.vtt

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

